		<r3d:repositoryName language="eng">dharmae</r3d:repositoryName>
				<r3d:additionalName language="eng">Data Hub of Australian Research on Marine &amp; Aquatic Ecocultures</r3d:additionalName>
				<r3d:repositoryUrl>https://dharmae.research.uts.edu.au/</r3d:repositoryUrl>
				<r3d:description language="eng">In a changing climate, water raises increasingly complex challenges: concerning its quantity, quality, availability, allocation, use and significance as a habitat, resource and cultural medium. Dharmae, a ‘Data Hub of Australian Research on Marine and Aquatic Ecocultures’ brings together multi-disciplinary research data relating to water in all these forms.
The term “ecoculture” guides the development of this collection and its approach to data discovery. Ecoculture recognizes that, since nature and culture are inextricably linked, there is a corresponding need for greater interconnectedness of the different knowledge systems applied to them.</r3d:description>
